APX.za = {"country":{"name":"South Africa","tagline":"Three and a half centuries of Cape wine, from Van Riebeeck's first pressing to Swartland old-vine Chenin, told in mountains, wind and granite.","classification":"The Wine of Origin (WO) scheme, in force since 1973 and administered by the Wine and Spirit Board, certifies three claims on a label: origin, grape variety and vintage. If a variety or vintage is named, at least 85 percent of the wine must be that variety or year; an origin claim requires 100 percent of the grapes from the named area. Every certified bottle carries a numbered seal.\n\nOrigins nest in a hierarchy that has grown more complex over time. The February 2026 list starts with the overarching geographical unit Greater Cape (Western, Northern and Eastern Cape) and six other geographical units (KwaZulu-Natal, Free State, Limpopo, North West and, oddly, a 'none' unit for the Lanseria ward). Inside the Western Cape are the overarching region Cape Coast (Coastal Region plus Cape South Coast) and the regions Breede River Valley, Klein Karoo and Olifants River; the Northern Cape holds the Karoo-Hoogland region. A newer subregion layer, Cape West Coast, groups Darling, Lutzville Valley, St Helena Bay and the coastal wards. Below these are districts (for example Stellenbosch, Paarl, Swartland, Walker Bay) and, at the smallest scale, wards (Simonsberg-Stellenbosch, Hemel-en-Aarde Valley, Piekenierskloof). Some wards sit outside any district (Cederberg, Elim's neighbours Napier and Herbertsdale, Lamberts Bay). In total WOSA counts 32 districts and about 100 wards.\n\nUnits are defined mostly by geography rather than by proven style, and like the Australian and New Zealand systems the scheme sets no rules on varieties or yields. Two other labels matter: 'Estate Wine', a term for wine grown, made and bottled on registered contiguous land, and the Old Vine Project's Certified Heritage Vineyard seal, which gives the planting year of vineyards at least 35 years old. The Integrated Production of Wine (IPW) sustainability scheme can be combined with the WO seal. 'Cape Port' and 'Cape Sherry' terms were retired under the EU trade agreement from 2012: fortified styles are now labelled Cape Vintage, Cape Ruby, Cape Tawny and Cape White, and Boberg is a historic designation for fortified wines from Paarl, Franschhoek and Tulbagh."},"regions":[{"name":"Coastal Region","slug":"coastal-region","tagline":"Stellenbosch, Paarl, Swartland and Constantia: the historic heart of Cape wine, within an hour of Cape Town.","ids":["za-agter-paarl","za-banghoek","za-blouvlei","za-bottelary","za-bovlei","za-cape-coast","za-cape-town","za-coastal-region","za-constantia","za-devon-valley","za-durbanville","za-franschhoek","za-groenberg","za-hout-bay","za-jonkershoek-valley","za-limietberg","za-malmesbury","za-mid-berg-river","za-paardeberg-south","za-paardeberg-perdeberg","za-paarl","za-papegaaiberg","za-philadelphia","za-piket-bo-berg","za-polkadraai-hills","za-porseleinberg","za-riebeekberg","za-riebeeksrivier","za-simonsberg-paarl","za-simonsberg-stellenbosch","za-stellenbosch","za-swartland","za-tulbagh","za-vlottenburg","za-voor-paardeberg","za-wellington"]},{"name":"Cape South Coast","slug":"cape-south-coast","tagline":"The cool southern rim of Africa, where Pinot Noir and Chardonnay found a home.","ids":["za-bot-river","za-buffeljags","za-cape-agulhas","za-cape-south-coast","za-elandskloof-kaaimansgat","za-elgin","za-elim","za-goukou-river-valley","za-greyton","za-hemel-en-aarde-ridge","za-hemel-en-aarde-valley","za-herbertsdale","za-klein-river","za-lower-duivenhoks-river","za-malgas","za-napier","za-overberg","za-plettenberg-bay","za-shaws-mountain","za-springfontein-rim","za-stanford-foothills","za-still-bay","za-stormsvlei","za-sundays-glen","za-swellendam","za-theewater","za-upper-hemel-en-aarde-valley","za-walker-bay"]},{"name":"Breede River Valley","slug":"breede-river-valley","tagline":"The broad, irrigated engine of Cape wine and brandy, with Robertson's limestone as its fine-wine jewel.","ids":["za-agterkliphoogte","za-ashton","za-boesmansrivier","za-bonnievale","za-breede-river-valley","za-breedekloof","za-eilandia","za-goedemoed","za-goree","za-goudini","za-goudmyn","za-hex-river-valley","za-hoopsrivier","za-keeromsberg","za-klaasvoogds","za-le-chasseur","za-mcgregor","za-moordkuil","za-nuy","za-robertson","za-rooikrans","za-scherpenheuvel","za-slanghoek","za-stettyn","za-vinkrivier","za-worcester","za-zandrivier"]},{"name":"Klein Karoo","slug":"klein-karoo","tagline":"Ostrich farms, mountain passes and South Africa's finest port-style wines.","ids":["za-calitzdorp","za-cango-valley","za-groenfontein","za-klein-karoo","za-koo-plateau","za-langeberg-garcia","za-montagu","za-outeniqua","za-tradouw","za-tradouw-highlands","za-upper-langkloof"]},{"name":"Olifants River","slug":"olifants-river","tagline":"From the high sandstone of Piekenierskloof to the huge co-operatives of Vredendal.","ids":["za-citrusdal-mountain","za-citrusdal-valley","za-olifants-river","za-piekenierskloof","za-spruitdrift","za-vredendal"]},{"name":"Northern Cape","slug":"northern-cape","tagline":"Desert vineyards on the Orange River and the highest vines in South Africa at Sutherland.","ids":["za-central-orange-river","za-douglas","za-groblershoop","za-grootdrink","za-hartswater","za-kakamas","za-karoo-hoogland","za-keimoes","za-northern-cape","za-prieska","za-sutherland-karoo","za-upington"]},{"name":"Cape West Coast","slug":"cape-west-coast","tagline":"Fog, cold Atlantic air and some of the Cape's most windswept vineyards.","ids":["za-bamboes-bay","za-cape-west-coast","za-darling","za-groenekloof","za-koekenaap","za-lamberts-bay","za-lutzville-valley","za-st-helena-bay"]},{"name":"National and multi-region","slug":"national-and-multi-region","tagline":"","ids":["za-cederberg","za-central-drakensberg","za-ceres","za-ceres-plateau","za-eastern-cape","za-free-state","za-greater-cape","za-kwazulu-natal","za-kweekvallei","za-lanseria","za-leipoldtville-sandveld","za-limpopo","za-lions-river","za-nieuwoudtville","za-north-west","za-nuveld-karoo","za-prince-albert","za-prince-albert-valley","za-rietrivier-fs","za-st-francis-bay","za-swartberg","za-western-cape"]}],"items":{"za-agter-paarl":{"name":"Agter-Paarl","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Paarl","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Pinotage, Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"The country 'behind' (agter) Paarl Mountain to the west, towards the Swartland, where Fairview's Charles Back farms goats and vines and makes Rhône-style wines and cheese. It is warmer and drier than the Paarl valley.","terroir":"Granite-derived soils and shale on gentle slopes; warm and dry.","producers":["Fairview","Spice Route (sources)"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-agterkliphoogte":{"name":"Agterkliphoogte","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward in the Agterkliphoogte valley near Robertson. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-ashton":{"name":"Ashton","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward around the town of Ashton at the foot of the Langeberg. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-bamboes-bay":{"name":"Bamboes Bay","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape West Coast","subregion":"Cape West Coast","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"One of South Africa's smallest wards, on the Atlantic coast north of Lamberts Bay, where Fryer's Cove's vineyards lie a few hundred metres from the ocean. Its Sauvignon Blanc is lean and saline.","terroir":"Sandy and limestone soils, cold Benguela fog.","producers":["Fryer's Cove"],"rslug":"cape-west-coast"},"za-banghoek":{"name":"Banghoek","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Stellenbosch","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Cabernet Franc, Merlot, Chardonnay","summary":"A high mountain bowl at the top of the Helshoogte Pass between Stellenbosch and Franschhoek, surrounded by the Simonsberg, Jonkershoek and Groot Drakenstein ranges. Cooler and wetter than the valley below, it gives fresh, elegant Bordeaux varieties and Chardonnay.","terroir":"Granite and sandstone soils at about 400 to 600 m; high rainfall.","producers":["Delaire Graff","Oldenburg Vineyards","Zorgvliet","Thelema (Banghoek holdings)"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-blouvlei":{"name":"Blouvlei","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Wellington","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinotage, Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward of the Wellington district on the slopes and plain below the Hawequa mountains. It is one of five Wellington wards on the February 2026 Wine of Origin list; most producers still label their wine WO Wellington.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-boesmansrivier":{"name":"Boesmansrivier","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward along the Boesmans River near Bonnievale. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-bonnievale":{"name":"Bonnievale","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward around Bonnievale on the Breede River, known for dairy and wine co-operatives. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-bot-river":{"name":"Bot River","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Walker Bay","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Pinotage, Shiraz, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"The gateway to Walker Bay, from the Bot River lagoon into the foothills of the Groenlandberg and Babylonstoren ranges, bordering the Kogelberg Biosphere. Beaumont, in the village, has old Chenin and Pinotage; Gabrielskloof, Wildekrans and Barton are nearby. Afternoon winds blow up the valley off the sea.","terroir":"Mainly Bokkeveld shale (Glen Rosa and Klapmuts soils) and Table Mountain sandstone.","producers":["Beaumont","Gabrielskloof","Wildekrans","Barton","Luddite"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-bottelary":{"name":"Bottelary","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Stellenbosch","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinotage, Chenin Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"The Bottelary Hills north-west of Stellenbosch, a ridge of granite with views to Table Mountain, is old-vine Chenin and Pinotage country. Bellevue, in these hills, made the Pinotage that won the 1959 Cape Wine Show, and Kaapzicht, Hartenberg, Mooiplaas and Bellevue still farm old bush vines.","terroir":"Decomposed granite on the upper slopes and shale lower down; open to Atlantic breezes from the west.","producers":["Kaapzicht","Hartenberg","Bellevue","Mooiplaas","Groenland"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-bovlei":{"name":"Bovlei","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Wellington","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinotage, Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward of Wellington in the upper Bovlei valley towards the Bainskloof Pass, home of the historic Bovlei co-operative cellar (1907). It is one of five Wellington wards on the February 2026 Wine of Origin list; most producers still label their wine WO Wellington.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-breede-river-valley":{"name":"Breede River Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Region","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white","sparkling","fortified"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Chardonnay, Shiraz","summary":"The inland region of the Breedekloof, Worcester and Robertson districts, warm and irrigated, the source of a large share of South Africa's wine and brandy. The region crushes a large share of South Africa's grapes, most of it through co-operative cellars.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-breedekloof":{"name":"Breedekloof","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Breede River Valley","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Pinotage, Shiraz","summary":"A district around Rawsonville in the upper Breede River and its tributaries, below the Du Toitskloof mountains. Its large co-operatives once sent most fruit to distillers; now cellars such as Badsberg, Slanghoek and Goudini bottle good-value Chenin, and its old vineyards are sought by Stellenbosch winemakers.","terroir":"Alluvial valley soils on a bed of river stones; varied mesoclimates in side valleys.","producers":["Badsberg","Slanghoek","Goudini","Merwida","Opstal"],"contains":["Goudini","Slanghoek"],"rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-buffeljags":{"name":"Buffeljags","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Swellendam","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard","summary":"A ward around the Buffeljags River and dam east of Swellendam. It sits in warm, dry country along the lower Breede River system, between the Robertson valley and the coast, and most of its grapes are sold in bulk.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-calitzdorp":{"name":"Calitzdorp","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["fortified","red","white"],"grapes":"Touriga Nacional, Tinta Barocca, Souzão, Muscat, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A small Klein Karoo town that calls itself South Africa's port capital. The Nel cousins at Boplaas and De Krans, and Axe Hill, make fortified wines from Portuguese varieties in Cape Vintage, Cape Tawny and Cape Ruby styles, the names used since 'port' was retired under the EU agreement in 2012. Hot days, cold nights and low rainfall concentrate the grapes. Its ward is Groenfontein.","terroir":"Alluvial and shale soils along the Gamka River; about 200 to 300 mm of rain.","producers":["Boplaas","De Krans","Axe Hill","Calitzdorp Cellar"],"contains":["Groenfontein"],"rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-cango-valley":{"name":"Cango Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["red","white","fortified"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Muscadel","summary":"A ward north of Oudtshoorn in the valley of the Cango Caves. It lies in the hot Oudtshoorn ostrich country.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-cape-agulhas":{"name":"Cape Agulhas","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Sémillon, Shiraz","summary":"The district at Africa's southern tip; almost all its vines are in the Elim ward. Strong winds and a cool ripening season produce pungent Sauvignon Blanc and Sémillon.","contains":["Elim"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-cape-coast":{"name":"Cape Coast","cat":"WO","subcat":"Overarching region","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Chenin Blanc, Shiraz, Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Noir","summary":"An overarching region that combines the Coastal Region and Cape South Coast, allowing blends of, say, Stellenbosch and Elgin fruit to name a coastal origin. It is a recent addition to the Wine of Origin hierarchy, sitting between the Western Cape unit and the regions.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-cape-south-coast":{"name":"Cape South Coast","cat":"WO","subcat":"Region","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape Coast","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay, Pinot Noir, Shiraz","summary":"The cool southern coastal region from Elgin to Plettenberg Bay, home to Walker Bay and its Hemel-en-Aarde wards, Elim and Elgin. Most of its vineyards are young, planted from the 1970s onward, and it is South Africa's main source of Pinot Noir.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-cape-town":{"name":"Cape Town","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Coastal Region","styles":["red","white","sparkling","sweet"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Muscat de Frontignan","summary":"A district named after the city, combining the wards of Constantia, Durbanville, Hout Bay and Philadelphia and the vineyards of the Cape Peninsula, including Cape Point. At its farthest point it is 36 km from the city centre. It replaced the former Cape Point and Tygerberg districts, which no longer appear on the February 2026 list.","terroir":"Sea on three sides, Table Mountain sandstone and granite, and the cooling south-easter; one of the coolest districts in South Africa.","producers":["Groot Constantia","Klein Constantia","Cape Point Vineyards","Diemersdal"],"contains":["Constantia","Durbanville","Hout Bay","Philadelphia"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-cape-west-coast":{"name":"Cape West Coast","cat":"WO","subcat":"Subregion","region":"Cape West Coast","subregion":"Coastal Region","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chenin Blanc, Pinotage","summary":"A subregion grouping the Atlantic-facing Darling and Lutzville Valley districts, St Helena Bay and the Bamboes Bay and Lamberts Bay wards, all cooled by the Benguela current. It was proposed in 2019 and appears on the February 2026 list of production areas.","rslug":"cape-west-coast"},"za-cederberg":{"name":"Cederberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chenin Blanc, Shiraz, Chardonnay","summary":"A stand-alone ward in the Cederberg wilderness, with some of South Africa's highest and remotest vineyards at about 950 to 1,100 m. The Nieuwoudt family's Cederberg Private Cellar at Dwarsrivier, planted in the 1970s, makes crisp Sauvignon, Chenin and Shiraz.","terroir":"Sandy soils from Table Mountain sandstone; cold winters with snow, hot dry summers.","producers":["Cederberg Private Cellar"],"rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-central-drakensberg":{"name":"Central Drakensberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"KwaZulu-Natal","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A district in the foothills of the Drakensberg near Winterton. Its vineyards at about 1,000 m face summer rainfall and hail.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-central-orange-river":{"name":"Central Orange River","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Northern Cape","styles":["red","white","sweet"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Muscat d'Alexandrie, Pinotage, Shiraz","summary":"The most northerly winegrowing area of the Cape, along about 350 km of the Orange River around Upington, Keimoes and Kakamas. Changed from a ward to a district after a 2019 proposal, it has five wards. About 6,000 ha are planted, largely for white wine, using high hut, gable and T-trellises that shade the grapes; vineyards on river islands are cooled by the water.","terroir":"Alluvial river soils; very hot and arid, fully irrigated.","producers":["Orange River Cellars"],"contains":["Groblershoop","Grootdrink","Kakamas","Keimoes","Upington"],"rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-ceres":{"name":"Ceres","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Ceres Plateau","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A ward in the Ceres valley and plateau, high and cold in winter. Its high, cool vineyards produce Chenin Blanc and Sauvignon Blanc prized for freshness, and the district is otherwise known for apples and pears.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-ceres-plateau":{"name":"Ceres Plateau","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Noir","summary":"A high plateau north-east of Ceres at about 1,000 m, apple and pear country whose cool vineyards supply sought-after Chenin and Pinot to Cape producers. It is one of the coldest wine districts in the Western Cape, with snow in winter.","contains":["Ceres"],"rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-citrusdal-mountain":{"name":"Citrusdal Mountain","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Olifants River","subregion":"Olifants River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Grenache, Chenin Blanc, Palomino, Pinotage","summary":"The mountain district above the Citrusdal valley, whose old, dry-farmed bush vines on sandstone are among the most prized in the new South Africa. Its ward is Piekenierskloof, and its high Skurfberg vineyards supply Chenin to Sadie, Alheit and others.","terroir":"Sandy, Table Mountain sandstone soils at up to 1,000 m; dry and hot by day, cold at night.","producers":["Alheit (Magnetic North)","Sadie Family (Skurfberg)"],"contains":["Piekenierskloof"],"rslug":"olifants-river"},"za-citrusdal-valley":{"name":"Citrusdal Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Olifants River","subregion":"Olifants River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Pinotage","summary":"The citrus-growing southern Olifants River valley around Citrusdal and Clanwilliam, irrigated from the Clanwilliam Dam. Its irrigated vineyards supply large cellars; the old dry-farmed vines that excite new-wave producers are in the mountains above.","rslug":"olifants-river"},"za-coastal-region":{"name":"Coastal Region","cat":"WO","subcat":"Region","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Cape Coast","styles":["red","white","sparkling","fortified","sweet"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Chenin Blanc, Shiraz, Pinotage, Merlot, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"The Coastal Region includes South Africa's best-known districts: Cape Town, Stellenbosch, Paarl, Franschhoek, Wellington, Swartland, Tulbagh, Darling and Lutzville Valley. 'WO Coastal Region' usually indicates a blend across several of them.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-constantia":{"name":"Constantia","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Cape Town","created":"1973 (Wine of Origin scheme)","styles":["white","red","sweet","sparkling"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Sémillon, Chardonnay, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Muscat de Frontignan","summary":"Constantia is the cradle of Cape wine and the source of one of history's most famous sweet wines. Simon van der Stel was granted the land in 1685 and planted a large vineyard on the eastern slopes of the Constantiaberg; after his death in 1712 the estate was split into Groot Constantia, Klein Constantia and Bergvliet. From 1778 Hendrik Cloete made an unfortified wine from late-picked Muscat de Frontignan (with some Pontac, Muscadel and Chenin) that European kings, Napoleon on St Helena, Jane Austen's characters and Baudelaire's verse all celebrated. Phylloxera and the end of imperial preference ended it in the late nineteenth century; Klein Constantia revived it as Vin de Constance in 1986, followed by Groot Constantia (Grand Constance) and Buitenverwachting.\n\nToday the ward's handful of estates, now surrounded by expensive suburbs, make some of South Africa's best Sauvignon Blanc and Sauvignon-Sémillon blends, aided by sea air from False Bay a few kilometres away. The ward also carries a modern history: under the Group Areas Act, Constantia was declared a white area in 1961 and families of colour were forcibly removed; the Solomon family won back its land through a restitution claim in 2010.","terroir":"East- and south-east-facing slopes of the Constantiaberg on decomposed granite and sandstone, about 1,000 mm of rain a year, and a mean February temperature of about 20.6 degrees C; cool sea breezes from False Bay.","producers":["Klein Constantia","Groot Constantia","Buitenverwachting","Steenberg","Constantia Glen","Eagles' Nest","Constantia Uitsig","Beau Constantia","Silvermist"],"nerd_note":"Klein Constantia's Vin de Constance bottle reproduces a squat, hand-blown 18th-century design, and it is aged about four years before release.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-darling":{"name":"Darling","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape West Coast","subregion":"Cape West Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Pinotage, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"Darling, an hour north of Cape Town on the west coast, is famous for spring wild flowers and for cool Sauvignon Blanc. Its Groenekloof ward is one of the closest in South Africa to the cold Atlantic.","terroir":"Decomposed granite hills catching Atlantic fog and wind.","producers":["Groote Post","Darling Cellars","Ormonde","Cloof"],"contains":["Groenekloof"],"rslug":"cape-west-coast"},"za-devon-valley":{"name":"Devon Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Stellenbosch","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Merlot, Pinotage, Cabernet Sauvignon, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A small, sheltered valley north-west of Stellenbosch town between the Bottelary Hills and Papegaaiberg, known for Merlot and Pinotage on granite and shale soils. It is one of the most sheltered parts of the district, and its small size keeps it a district of family estates.","terroir":"Granite-derived soils, sheltered from wind.","producers":["Clos Malverne","Louisvale","Meinert"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-douglas":{"name":"Douglas","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Northern Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A district around Douglas, near the confluence of the Orange and Vaal rivers, with irrigated vineyards. Like the Central Orange River vineyards, it depends on irrigation in a hot, arid climate.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-durbanville":{"name":"Durbanville","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Cape Town","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon, Chardonnay, Pinotage","summary":"Rolling wheat-and-vine country on the northern edge of Cape Town, whose hills catch Atlantic breezes and night-time mist. Durbanville made its name for pungent, green-fruited Sauvignon Blanc and soft Merlot, and many farms (Diemersdal, Meerendal, Altydgedacht) have been in the same families for generations.","terroir":"Deep, red, decomposed granite and shale soils that hold water, allowing dry farming; vineyards up to about 380 m.","producers":["Diemersdal","Durbanville Hills","Nitida","Altydgedacht","Meerendal","De Grendel"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-eastern-cape":{"name":"Eastern Cape","cat":"WO","subcat":"Geographical Unit","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Greater Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay, Pinot Noir","summary":"The Eastern Cape was designated a geographical unit in 2009. Its only ward is St Francis Bay, on the coast west of Port Elizabeth (Gqeberha). Its few vineyards face rain spread through the year, unlike the Western Cape's dry summers.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-eilandia":{"name":"Eilandia","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward on low-lying land along the Breede River between Robertson and Ashton. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-elandskloof-kaaimansgat":{"name":"Elandskloof/Kaaimansgat","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Overberg","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Pinot Noir","summary":"A high, cool ward in the mountains near Villiersdorp. Bouchard Finlayson's Kaaimansgat ('crocodile's lair') Chardonnay comes from vineyards here at around 700 m. It is one of the coolest Chardonnay sites in the Cape.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-elgin":{"name":"Elgin","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay, Pinot Noir, Riesling, Shiraz","summary":"Elgin is a high basin about an hour east of Cape Town, ringed by the Hottentots Holland mountains, which grew most of South Africa's apples before its farmers began planting vines in the late 1980s. Its altitude (200 to 800 m), cloud and proximity to the sea make it one of the coolest districts in South Africa, and its Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Noir are taut and fine. Paul Cluver, Oak Valley, Iona, Richard Kershaw and Shannon lead.","terroir":"Table Mountain sandstone and Bokkeveld shale; cool summers, about 1,000 mm of rain.","producers":["Paul Cluver","Oak Valley","Iona","Richard Kershaw","Shannon","Almenkerk","Elgin Vintners"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-elim":{"name":"Elim","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape Agulhas","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Sémillon, Shiraz, Pinot Noir","summary":"Elim's vineyards lie near Cape Agulhas, Africa's southernmost point, around the Moravian mission village of Elim, founded in 1824 and a national monument. Strong summer winds and a very cool ripening season give pungent, mineral Sauvignon Blanc and Sémillon and peppery Shiraz.","terroir":"Ferricrete, shale and sandstone soils; constant wind off the sea.","producers":["Strandveld","The Berrio","Black Oystercatcher","Trizanne Signature (sources)"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-franschhoek":{"name":"Franschhoek","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Coastal Region","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Sémillon, Chardonnay, Cabernet Sauvignon, Chenin Blanc, Pinot Noir","summary":"Franschhoek, the 'French corner', is the valley where the VOC settled Huguenot refugees after 1688. It is enclosed on three sides by the Groot Drakenstein and Franschhoek mountains, with the Berg River rising at its head. The district holds some of South Africa's oldest vineyards, including Sémillon (and the rare Sémillon Gris) planted in the early twentieth century, and it is a centre of Cap Classique and of the Cape's restaurant culture. The Huguenot Monument (1948) stands at the head of the town.","terroir":"Sandy alluvium on the valley floor and decomposed sandstone and granite on the slopes; enclosed, warmer by day and colder at night than Stellenbosch, with snow on the peaks in winter.","producers":["Boekenhoutskloof","La Motte","Chamonix","Haute Cabrière","Mont Rochelle","Leeu Passant","Boschendal (nearby)","Graham Beck (historic cellar)"],"nerd_note":"Boekenhoutskloof's Sémillon comes from vines planted in 1902 and 1942, among the oldest Sémillon in the world.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-free-state":{"name":"Free State","cat":"WO","subcat":"Geographical Unit","region":"National and multi-region","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc","summary":"The Free State geographical unit has one ward, Rietrivier FS, on the Riet River near Jacobsdal. Grapes there are mostly grown for local co-operative wine and brandy.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-goedemoed":{"name":"Goedemoed","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward of the Robertson district. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-goree":{"name":"Goree","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward west of Robertson town. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-goudini":{"name":"Goudini","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Breedekloof","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard","summary":"A ward around Rawsonville in the Breedekloof. Its alluvial soils over river stones and the cooling effect of the surrounding mountains suit Chenin Blanc and Colombard, delivered mostly to the Goudini co-operative cellar.","producers":["Goudini Wines"],"rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-goudmyn":{"name":"Goudmyn","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward of the Robertson district. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-goukou-river-valley":{"name":"Goukou River Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Still Bay","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A ward along the Goukou River inland from Stilbaai. It is one of the most easterly coastal wine wards on the Garden Route, with a mild, wet maritime climate.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-greater-cape":{"name":"Greater Cape","cat":"WO","subcat":"Overarching geographical unit","region":"National and multi-region","styles":["red","white","sparkling","fortified","sweet"],"grapes":"All Cape varieties","summary":"An overarching unit created after a 2019 proposal that groups the Western Cape, Northern Cape and Eastern Cape geographical units, so that wines blended across provincial lines (for example Western Cape and Orange River fruit) can carry a Cape origin.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-greyton":{"name":"Greyton","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Overberg","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Pinot Noir, Syrah","summary":"A ward around the village of Greyton below the Riviersonderend mountains, where Samantha O'Keefe's Lismore Estate makes Chardonnay and Syrah. Its vineyards are cool and wind-exposed.","producers":["Lismore"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-groblershoop":{"name":"Groblershoop","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Central Orange River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc, Muscat","summary":"A ward on the Orange River around the town of Groblershoop in the Central Orange River district, an irrigated desert-oasis vineyard area. The Orange River vineyards ripen very early (harvest can start in December), and most grapes go to Orange River Cellars, one of the largest wine businesses in South Africa, for Colombard, Chenin Blanc, sweet Muscat and juice.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-groenberg":{"name":"Groenberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Wellington","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinotage, Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward around the Groenberg hill north of Wellington town, with granite soils. It is one of five Wellington wards on the February 2026 Wine of Origin list; most producers still label their wine WO Wellington.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-groenekloof":{"name":"Groenekloof","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape West Coast","subregion":"Darling","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Noir, Shiraz","summary":"The Darling ward nearest the Atlantic, whose Sauvignon Blanc, cooled by sea breezes and fog, spearheaded the area's development. Groote Post's Peter Pentz farms here. Neil Ellis was an early buyer of its cool-climate fruit.","terroir":"Granite-derived soils on hills a few kilometres from the sea.","producers":["Groote Post","Neil Ellis (Groenekloof Sauvignon)"],"rslug":"cape-west-coast"},"za-groenfontein":{"name":"Groenfontein","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Calitzdorp","styles":["red","white","fortified"],"grapes":"Touriga Nacional, Muscat","summary":"A ward in the Groenfontein valley north of Calitzdorp, below the Swartberg. Its vineyards supply Calitzdorp's port-style producers with Touriga Nacional, Tinta Barocca and Muscat, ripened in a hot, dry valley enclosed by mountains.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-grootdrink":{"name":"Grootdrink","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Central Orange River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc, Muscat","summary":"A ward on the Orange River around the town of Grootdrink in the Central Orange River district, an irrigated desert-oasis vineyard area. The Orange River vineyards ripen very early (harvest can start in December), and most grapes go to Orange River Cellars, one of the largest wine businesses in South Africa, for Colombard, Chenin Blanc, sweet Muscat and juice.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-hartswater":{"name":"Hartswater","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Northern Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A ward in the Vaalharts irrigation scheme in the far north of the Northern Cape. The scheme, one of the largest in the southern hemisphere, grows grain, pecans and grapes.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-hemel-en-aarde-ridge":{"name":"Hemel-en-Aarde Ridge","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Walker Bay","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinot Noir, Chardonnay, Syrah","summary":"The highest and furthest inland of the three Hemel-en-Aarde wards, at the top of the valley around 300 m and above, with cooler nights. Creation and Domaine des Dieux are here, and Chris and Suzaan Alheit's Hemelrand farm is nearby.","terroir":"Shale and sandstone with some granite; cool and windy.","producers":["Creation","Domaine des Dieux","Ataraxia"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-hemel-en-aarde-valley":{"name":"Hemel-en-Aarde Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Walker Bay","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinot Noir, Chardonnay, Pinotage, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"The lowest of the three Hemel-en-Aarde wards, closest to the sea at Hermanus. Hamilton Russell Vineyards (1975) and Bouchard Finlayson (1989, a venture between Peter Finlayson and Burgundy's Paul Bouchard) established South African Pinot Noir and Chardonnay here; the clay-rich shale soils give wines of structure and minerality.","terroir":"Bokkeveld shale with high clay content, stony; cool sea breezes, about 750 mm of rain.","producers":["Hamilton Russell","Bouchard Finlayson","Southern Right","Whalehaven"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-herbertsdale":{"name":"Herbertsdale","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A stand-alone ward near the village of Herbertsdale inland from Mossel Bay. Its mild Garden Route climate, with rain through the year, suits white varieties such as Sauvignon Blanc.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-hex-river-valley":{"name":"Hex River Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Worcester","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz","summary":"The Hex River Valley around De Doorns, South Africa's largest table-grape area, also grows wine grapes. It is one of seven wards in the Worcester district, a warm, irrigated area whose fruit goes largely to wine and brandy.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-hoopsrivier":{"name":"Hoopsrivier","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward of the Robertson district. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-hout-bay":{"name":"Hout Bay","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Cape Town","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay, Pinot Noir","summary":"One of South Africa's smallest wards, in the steep valley behind Hout Bay harbour on the Cape Peninsula, with a few hectares of vines. Its vines grow on steep slopes in sight of the Atlantic.","terroir":"Steep granite and sandstone slopes facing the Atlantic.","producers":["Hout Bay Vineyards"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-jonkershoek-valley":{"name":"Jonkershoek Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Stellenbosch","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Syrah, Chardonnay","summary":"A narrow, steep-sided valley running south-east from Stellenbosch town into the Jonkershoek mountains, one of the wettest and most enclosed parts of the district. Morning shade and late sun give long, slow ripening; Stark-Condé and Neil Ellis's Jonkershoek vineyards make fine, fresh Cabernet.","terroir":"Decomposed granite and sandstone colluvium on steep slopes; about 1,000 mm or more of rain.","producers":["Stark-Condé","Neil Ellis","Lanzerac","Oldenburg (nearby)"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-kakamas":{"name":"Kakamas","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Central Orange River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc, Muscat","summary":"A ward on the Orange River around the town of Kakamas in the Central Orange River district, an irrigated desert-oasis vineyard area. The Orange River vineyards ripen very early (harvest can start in December), and most grapes go to Orange River Cellars, one of the largest wine businesses in South Africa, for Colombard, Chenin Blanc, sweet Muscat and juice.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-karoo-hoogland":{"name":"Karoo-Hoogland","cat":"WO","subcat":"Region","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Northern Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Pinot Noir, Chardonnay","summary":"A high-plateau region in the Northern Cape whose only district is Sutherland-Karoo, around one of South Africa's coldest towns. Its vineyards, at around 1,500 m, are the highest in South Africa.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-keeromsberg":{"name":"Keeromsberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Worcester","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz","summary":"A ward named after the Keeromsberg mountain north of Worcester. It is one of seven wards in the Worcester district, a warm, irrigated area whose fruit goes largely to wine and brandy. Grapes from here go mainly to the Worcester district's co-operatives and to the brandy distilleries that make Worcester South Africa's brandy capital; ward names are rarely used on bottles.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-keimoes":{"name":"Keimoes","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Central Orange River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc, Muscat","summary":"A ward on the Orange River around the town of Keimoes in the Central Orange River district, an irrigated desert-oasis vineyard area. The Orange River vineyards ripen very early (harvest can start in December), and most grapes go to Orange River Cellars, one of the largest wine businesses in South Africa, for Colombard, Chenin Blanc, sweet Muscat and juice.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-klaasvoogds":{"name":"Klaasvoogds","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward in the foothills of the Langeberg north-east of Robertson. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-klein-karoo":{"name":"Klein Karoo","cat":"WO","subcat":"Region","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white","fortified","sweet"],"grapes":"Muscat, Touriga Nacional, Chenin Blanc, Colombard","summary":"The semi-arid valley along Route 62 from Montagu to the Langkloof, known for Calitzdorp's fortified wines, Muscadel and potstill brandy. Vines grow in kloofs and river valleys between ostrich farms.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-klein-river":{"name":"Klein River","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Overberg","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Pinotage","summary":"A ward near Stanford along the Klein River, where award-winning wines (Raka) have emerged. Its cool coastal climate suits Sauvignon Blanc and Bordeaux varieties.","producers":["Raka"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-koekenaap":{"name":"Koekenaap","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape West Coast","subregion":"Lutzville Valley","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A cool, sea-influenced ward close to the Atlantic in the Lutzville Valley, where grapes ripen slowly in coastal fog. It is one of the most northerly coastal wards in South Africa.","rslug":"cape-west-coast"},"za-koo-plateau":{"name":"Koo Plateau","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Pinot Noir","summary":"A high plateau north of Montagu at about 1,000 m, apple and pear country with a cool climate. Its cool upland climate attracts winemakers looking for fresh Chenin Blanc.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-kwazulu-natal":{"name":"KwaZulu-Natal","cat":"WO","subcat":"Geographical Unit","region":"National and multi-region","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon, Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay","summary":"KwaZulu-Natal, designated in 2005, stretches from Greytown to the Midlands at up to about 1,500 m. Its summer rainfall makes viticulture difficult; it contains the Lions River and Central Drakensberg districts.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-kweekvallei":{"name":"Kweekvallei","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Prince Albert","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz","summary":"A small ward near Prince Albert in the Karoo. Its irrigated vineyards grow small quantities of Shiraz and other reds in a hot, dry climate at the foot of the Swartberg mountains.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-lamberts-bay":{"name":"Lamberts Bay","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape West Coast","subregion":"Cape West Coast","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A coastal ward around the fishing town of Lamberts Bay, cooled by the Benguela current. Its vineyards, among the coolest on the west coast, mostly grow Sauvignon Blanc.","rslug":"cape-west-coast"},"za-langeberg-garcia":{"name":"Langeberg-Garcia","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A district along the Langeberg range around the Garcia Pass near Riversdale. Its few vineyards lie at the eastern end of the Langeberg, on the edge of the Klein Karoo, with a cooler, wetter climate than the valleys to the north.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-lanseria":{"name":"Lanseria","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward near Lanseria, north-west of Johannesburg in Gauteng, listed under no geographical unit on the February 2026 schedule; it is one of the few demarcated wine areas in South Africa's interior highveld.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-le-chasseur":{"name":"Le Chasseur","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward of the Robertson district north of the town. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-leipoldtville-sandveld":{"name":"Leipoldtville-Sandveld","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A ward in the sandy coastal plain (Sandveld) around Leipoldtville, west of Clanwilliam. Its sandy soils and cool Atlantic influence suit Sauvignon Blanc and Chenin Blanc.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-limietberg":{"name":"Limietberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Wellington","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinotage, Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward on the lower slopes of the Limietberg (Hawequa) range east of Wellington, where mountain foothills create cooler mesoclimates. It is one of five Wellington wards on the February 2026 Wine of Origin list; most producers still label their wine WO Wellington.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-limpopo":{"name":"Limpopo","cat":"WO","subcat":"Geographical Unit","region":"National and multi-region","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"A geographical unit covering South Africa's northernmost province; it has no regions, districts or wards on the February 2026 list. Summer rainfall and subtropical heat make viticulture marginal.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-lions-river":{"name":"Lions River","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"KwaZulu-Natal","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay, Shiraz","summary":"A district in the KwaZulu-Natal Midlands near Howick, at about 1,000 to 1,200 m. Summer rainfall makes viticulture challenging, but cool nights suit Sauvignon Blanc and Chardonnay.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-lower-duivenhoks-river":{"name":"Lower Duivenhoks River","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A small district along the lower Duivenhoks River between Heidelberg and the coast at Witsand. Its few vineyards benefit from sea breezes off the Indian Ocean near Witsand.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-lutzville-valley":{"name":"Lutzville Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape West Coast","subregion":"Cape West Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Sauvignon Blanc, Colombard","summary":"A district near the mouth of the Olifants River with large irrigated vineyards, including the Lutzville co-operative. It is one of the most northerly coastal wine districts in South Africa, cooled by the Atlantic and dependent on irrigation from the Olifants River.","producers":["Lutzville Vineyards"],"contains":["Koekenaap"],"rslug":"cape-west-coast"},"za-malgas":{"name":"Malgas","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Swellendam","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Syrah, Mourvèdre, Touriga Nacional, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A pioneering ward on a stony plateau 80 km east of Cape Agulhas, about 70 m above the Breede River. David and Rita Trafford's Sijnn planted drought-tolerant Mediterranean varieties here; rainfall is only about 350 mm, moderated by sea breezes from the coast 15 km away.","terroir":"Complex stony soils of shale and quartzite gravel.","producers":["Sijnn"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-malmesbury":{"name":"Malmesbury","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Swartland","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinotage, Shiraz, Chenin Blanc","summary":"The ward around Malmesbury, the Swartland's main town, among wheatfields on Malmesbury shale. Its old dryland bush vines of Chenin Blanc and Pinotage were long sold to the Swartland Winery co-operative and are now sought by smaller producers too.","producers":["Swartland Winery"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-mcgregor":{"name":"McGregor","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward around the village of McGregor, south of Robertson below the Riviersonderend mountains, cooler and drier than the valley floor. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-mid-berg-river":{"name":"Mid-Berg River","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Wellington","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinotage, Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward on the alluvial terraces of the middle Berg River between Wellington and Paarl. It is one of five Wellington wards on the February 2026 Wine of Origin list; most producers still label their wine WO Wellington.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-montagu":{"name":"Montagu","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["red","white","fortified"],"grapes":"Muscadel, Chenin Blanc, Colombard","summary":"A ward around the spa town of Montagu at the western gateway of the Klein Karoo, famous for its fortified Muscadel. Its Muscadel is made from red and white Muscat à Petits Grains, fortified to sweetness.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-moordkuil":{"name":"Moordkuil","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Worcester","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz","summary":"A ward of the Worcester district. It is one of seven wards in the Worcester district, a warm, irrigated area whose fruit goes largely to wine and brandy. Grapes from here go mainly to the Worcester district's co-operatives and to the brandy distilleries that make Worcester South Africa's brandy capital; ward names are rarely used on bottles.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-napier":{"name":"Napier","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A stand-alone ward around the Overberg village of Napier, between Bredasdorp and Caledon. Like nearby Elim, it is cooled by winds off the sea near Africa's southern tip, which suits Sauvignon Blanc and Shiraz.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-nieuwoudtville":{"name":"Nieuwoudtville","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc","summary":"A ward around the town of Nieuwoudtville on the Bokkeveld plateau, known for spring wild flowers, at the north-western edge of the Cape. Its vineyards are cool and high, at about 750 m.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-north-west":{"name":"North West","cat":"WO","subcat":"Geographical Unit","region":"National and multi-region","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"A geographical unit covering the North West province; it has no regions, districts or wards on the February 2026 list. Summer rainfall and highveld frost make viticulture marginal.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-northern-cape":{"name":"Northern Cape","cat":"WO","subcat":"Geographical Unit","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Greater Cape","styles":["red","white","sweet"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc, Muscat d'Alexandrie, Pinotage","summary":"The Northern Cape geographical unit covers the irrigated vineyards of the Orange River and the high Karoo around Sutherland. Most fruit goes to large co-operative cellars. Its best-known wine area is the Central Orange River district around Upington, where vineyards on islands in the river are cooled by the water.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-nuveld-karoo":{"name":"Nuveld-Karoo","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white"],"summary":"A district on the high Karoo plateau inland of the Cape fold mountains, listed on the February 2026 schedule with no wards. Its vineyards are among the most remote in South Africa.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-nuy":{"name":"Nuy","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Worcester","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz","summary":"A small valley east of Worcester whose Nuy cellar is famous for fortified Muscadel. It is one of seven wards in the Worcester district, a warm, irrigated area whose fruit goes largely to wine and brandy.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-olifants-river":{"name":"Olifants River","cat":"WO","subcat":"Region","region":"Olifants River","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Grenache, Pinotage","summary":"The region along the Olifants River from Citrusdal to Lutzville, with old mountain vineyards at Piekenierskloof and large irrigated cellars at Vredendal. It is citrus and rooibos country.","rslug":"olifants-river"},"za-outeniqua":{"name":"Outeniqua","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinot Noir, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz","summary":"A ward in the Outeniqua mountains north of George, where vineyards on the Montagu Pass reach about 700 m. Its vineyards near George get rain through the year and cooler temperatures than the Klein Karoo valleys to the north.","producers":["Herold"],"rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-overberg":{"name":"Overberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Noir","summary":"A broad district of wheatfields and mountains east of Elgin, with wards at Elandskloof/Kaaimansgat, Greyton, Klein River, Shaw's Mountain and Theewater. Its cool, high wards produce Chardonnay, Pinot Noir and Sauvignon Blanc.","contains":["Elandskloof/Kaaimansgat","Greyton","Klein River","Shaw's Mountain","Theewater"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-paardeberg-perdeberg":{"name":"Paardeberg/Perdeberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Swartland","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Shiraz, Grenache, Cinsault, Mourvèdre","summary":"The granite massif of the Paardeberg (Perdeberg in Afrikaans), on the border of the Swartland and Paarl, is the spiritual home of the Swartland revival. Eben Sadie's farm and cellar, A.A. Badenhorst's Kalmoesfontein and many old Chenin and Cinsault vineyards are here. Its decomposed granite holds winter rain, so old bush vines survive without irrigation.","terroir":"Decomposed granite over clay on rounded hills; warm, dry and windy.","producers":["Sadie Family","A.A. Badenhorst","Perdeberg Wines","Lammershoek (nearby)"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-paardeberg-south":{"name":"Paardeberg South","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Swartland","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Shiraz, Pinotage","summary":"The southern foothills of the Paardeberg, separated as their own ward, with granite soils similar to the main Paardeberg ward. Old dry-farmed bush vines of Chenin Blanc and Cinsault here supply several new-wave Swartland labels.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-paarl":{"name":"Paarl","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Coastal Region","styles":["red","white","sparkling","fortified"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Shiraz, Pinotage, Chenin Blanc, Chardonnay","summary":"Paarl, named after the pearl-like granite domes of Paarl Mountain, lies north of Stellenbosch along the Berg River. It was the seat of the KWV from 1918, which made it the administrative capital of the industry for most of the twentieth century, and home to Nederburg, whose annual auction (from 1975) became the country's most important wine sale. The district is warmer than Stellenbosch and its Shiraz, Cabernet, Pinotage and Chenin are generous and ripe. Its wards are Simonsberg-Paarl, Voor-Paardeberg and Agter-Paarl.","terroir":"Granite domes and slopes, with alluvial soils along the Berg River; the valley needs supplementary irrigation in hot summers while the eastern slopes hold water.","producers":["Nederburg","KWV","Fairview","Glen Carlou","Backsberg","Avondale","Rupert & Rothschild","Plaisir de Merle"],"contains":["Simonsberg-Paarl","Voor-Paardeberg","Agter-Paarl"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-papegaaiberg":{"name":"Papegaaiberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Stellenbosch","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Shiraz, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A small hill just west of Stellenbosch town, the 'parrot mountain' where early settlers practised shooting at a wooden parrot. The Bergkelder, Distell's (now Heineken Beverages') maturation cellar, is tunnelled into its slopes.","terroir":"Granite and shale on a low ridge.","producers":["Bergkelder"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-philadelphia":{"name":"Philadelphia","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Cape Town","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A small ward north of Durbanville around the village of Philadelphia, on hills up to about 260 m within sight of the Atlantic, known for structured Bordeaux-style reds. Capaia, with its hilltop winery, is the ward's best-known estate.","terroir":"Weathered shale and granite; cool Atlantic influence with large day-night differences.","producers":["Capaia","Havana Hills"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-piekenierskloof":{"name":"Piekenierskloof","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Olifants River","subregion":"Citrusdal Mountain","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Grenache, Chenin Blanc, Palomino, Pinotage, Cinsault","summary":"A high plateau above the Piekenierskloof Pass south of Citrusdal, with some of South Africa's oldest Grenache and Palomino vineyards. Dry-farmed bush vines on deep sand give perfumed, light-coloured Grenache and textured whites prized by Swartland and Stellenbosch winemakers.","terroir":"Deep, sandy soils derived from sandstone at 600 to 750 m.","producers":["Piekenierskloof Wine Company","Sadie (Soldaat Grenache)","Org de Rac (nearby)"],"rslug":"olifants-river"},"za-piket-bo-berg":{"name":"Piket-Bo-Berg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Swartland","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz","summary":"A high plateau on top of the Piketberg mountain, north of the Swartland at about 600 to 700 m, cooler than the valleys below; the WOSA text calls it Piketberg-Bo-Berg.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-plettenberg-bay":{"name":"Plettenberg Bay","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay, Pinot Noir","summary":"The newest and furthest-east district on the Cape South Coast, in mountainous terrain about 20 km east of Plettenberg Bay. The first vines were planted in 2000 (Bramon, known for Cap Classique). Cool coastal climate and high-carbon soils suit Sauvignon Blanc and sparkling.","producers":["Bramon","Packwood","Kay & Monty"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-polkadraai-hills":{"name":"Polkadraai Hills","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Stellenbosch","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"Hills west of Stellenbosch near the R310 and Polkadraai Road, open to cool breezes from both False Bay and the Atlantic. Johan Reyneke farms biodynamically here, and the ward's sandy granite soils give fresh, fragrant Syrah and Chenin.","terroir":"Sandy, decomposed granite over clay at about 100 to 300 m.","producers":["Reyneke","Stellenbosch Hills","Mooiplaas (nearby)"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-porseleinberg":{"name":"Porseleinberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Swartland","styles":["red"],"grapes":"Syrah","summary":"A ward named after the 'porcelain mountain' between Riebeek-Kasteel and the Berg River, whose blue-grey schist soils Boekenhoutskloof chose for its Porseleinberg Syrah, farmed organically by Callie Louw since the first vintage in 2010.","terroir":"Malmesbury schist with very little topsoil; warm and dry.","producers":["Porseleinberg (Boekenhoutskloof)"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-prieska":{"name":"Prieska","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Northern Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A ward around Prieska on the Orange River. Its hot, dry vineyards are irrigated from the river and grow mainly white grapes for local cellars.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-prince-albert":{"name":"Prince Albert","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Western Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A district around the Karoo town of Prince Albert below the Swartberg, with the wards Kweekvallei, Prince Albert Valley and Swartberg. Its few vineyards make small volumes for local producers.","contains":["Kweekvallei","Prince Albert Valley","Swartberg"],"rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-prince-albert-valley":{"name":"Prince Albert Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Prince Albert","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Pinot Noir","summary":"A ward in the valley around Prince Albert, a hot, dry Karoo town at the foot of the Swartberg Pass. Its few hectares of vines are irrigated from mountain streams.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-riebeekberg":{"name":"Riebeekberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Swartland","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Grenache, Mourvèdre","summary":"The slopes of the Kasteelberg around the villages of Riebeek-Kasteel and Riebeek-West, where the Mullineuxs farm their Roundstone vineyard on schist and iron-rich soils. Many of the Swartland's new-wave producers source fruit here.","terroir":"Schist, shale and koffieklip (iron-rich ferricrete).","producers":["Mullineux","Kloovenburg","Riebeek Cellars"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-riebeeksrivier":{"name":"Riebeeksrivier","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Swartland","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A newer ward along the Riebeeks River valley below the Kasteelberg, on shale and alluvial soils. It lies between the Riebeekberg and Porseleinberg wards in the heart of the new-wave Swartland.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-rietrivier-fs":{"name":"Rietrivier FS","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Free State","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A ward on the Riet River near Jacobsdal in the Free State, home of the Landzicht cellar. It is one of the few demarcated wine areas in South Africa's interior.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-robertson":{"name":"Robertson","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Breede River Valley","styles":["red","white","sparkling","fortified"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon, Muscadel","summary":"The 'valley of vines and roses' along the Breede River is the only part of the Cape with significant lime-rich soils, which also suit its many racehorse studs. Hot summers are tempered by south-easterly winds that bring moist air up the valley. Danie de Wet of De Wetshof pioneered Chardonnay here in the 1970s, and Graham Beck's Madeba farm built South Africa's leading Cap Classique house in the 1990s. The district has 14 wards.","terroir":"Calcareous soils over limestone along the Breede, with alluvium; about 400 mm of rain, irrigation needed.","producers":["Graham Beck","De Wetshof","Springfield","Bon Courage","Van Loveren","Robertson Winery","Rietvallei"],"contains":["Agterkliphoogte","Ashton","Boesmansrivier","Bonnievale","Eilandia","Goedemoed","Goree","Goudmyn","Hoopsrivier","Klaasvoogds","Le Chasseur","McGregor","Vinkrivier","Zandrivier"],"rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-rooikrans":{"name":"Rooikrans","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Worcester","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz","summary":"A ward of the Worcester district. It is one of seven wards in the Worcester district, a warm, irrigated area whose fruit goes largely to wine and brandy. Grapes from here go mainly to the Worcester district's co-operatives and to the brandy distilleries that make Worcester South Africa's brandy capital; ward names are rarely used on bottles.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-scherpenheuvel":{"name":"Scherpenheuvel","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Worcester","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz","summary":"A ward on the road between Worcester and Robertson near the Brandvlei Dam. It is one of seven wards in the Worcester district, a warm, irrigated area whose fruit goes largely to wine and brandy.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-shaws-mountain":{"name":"Shaw's Mountain","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Overberg","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay","summary":"A recently added Overberg ward on the mountain slopes between Caledon and the Hemel-en-Aarde. Its cool, elevated slopes are suited to Sauvignon Blanc and Chardonnay.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-simonsberg-paarl":{"name":"Simonsberg-Paarl","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Paarl","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Shiraz, Chardonnay, Merlot","summary":"The north-eastern slopes of the Simonsberg facing Paarl, on decomposed granite. Glen Carlou, Plaisir de Merle, Backsberg and Rupert & Rothschild make Bordeaux blends and Chardonnay here. It is warmer than the Simonsberg-Stellenbosch side of the mountain, and its reds are correspondingly riper.","terroir":"Granite-derived soils on north- and east-facing slopes; warmer than the Stellenbosch side of the mountain.","producers":["Glen Carlou","Plaisir de Merle","Backsberg","Rupert & Rothschild","Noble Hill"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-simonsberg-stellenbosch":{"name":"Simonsberg-Stellenbosch","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Stellenbosch","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Pinotage, Merlot, Shiraz, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"The southern and western slopes of the granite Simonsberg (1,390 m) north-east of Stellenbosch, one of the most prestigious wards in South Africa and among the first to be demarcated. Its well-drained, red decomposed-granite soils, altitude and afternoon sea breezes give structured, long-lived Cabernet and Bordeaux blends and the country's most famous Pinotage. Kanonkop, Rustenberg, Thelema, Tokara, Warwick, Delheim and Uitkyk are all here.","terroir":"Decomposed granite (red Hutton and Clovelly soils) at about 150 to 500 m; south- and west-facing slopes catch the False Bay breeze.","producers":["Kanonkop","Rustenberg","Thelema","Tokara","Warwick","Delheim","Uitkyk","Morgenhof","Le Bonheur"],"nerd_note":"The official schedule of February 2026 misspells the ward as 'Simonsberg-Stellenbosh'.","rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-slanghoek":{"name":"Slanghoek","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Breedekloof","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Muscat","summary":"The Slanghoek valley north-west of Rawsonville, under the Slanghoek mountains. The Slanghoek cellar, a former co-operative, makes the ward's best-known wines, including fortified Hanepoot (Muscat d'Alexandrie) and Chenin Blanc.","producers":["Slanghoek"],"rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-springfontein-rim":{"name":"Springfontein Rim","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Walker Bay","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Pinotage, Pinot Noir","summary":"A small coastal ward near Stanford around the Springfontein estate, close to the sea on limestone-influenced soils. The Springfontein estate, owned by a German family, grows Chenin Blanc and Pinotage on limestone-influenced coastal soils there.","producers":["Springfontein"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-spruitdrift":{"name":"Spruitdrift","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Olifants River","subregion":"Olifants River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard","summary":"An irrigated ward on the lower Olifants River near Vredendal. Its grapes go mostly to the large Namaqua Wines cellar, for inexpensive whites and reds, and the hot, dry valley floor depends on irrigation from the Clanwilliam Dam.","rslug":"olifants-river"},"za-st-francis-bay":{"name":"St Francis Bay","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Eastern Cape","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Noir","summary":"The Eastern Cape's only ward, near the coastal resort of St Francis Bay. Its cool maritime climate suits Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Noir.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-st-helena-bay":{"name":"St Helena Bay","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape West Coast","subregion":"Swartland","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A coastal ward on St Helena Bay on the Atlantic, the fishing coast north of Saldanha, now grouped in the Cape West Coast subregion though listed under the Swartland district.","terroir":"Sandy soils, cold Benguela fog and wind.","rslug":"cape-west-coast"},"za-stanford-foothills":{"name":"Stanford Foothills","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Walker Bay","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chenin Blanc, Pinot Noir","summary":"A ward on the foothills of the Kleinrivier mountains above the village of Stanford, east of the Hemel-en-Aarde. It was registered as a ward recently, alongside Springfontein Rim and Sunday's Glen, as Walker Bay's vineyards spread east from the Hemel-en-Aarde.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-stellenbosch":{"name":"Stellenbosch","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Coastal Region","created":"1973 (Wine of Origin scheme)","styles":["red","white","sparkling","sweet"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Shiraz, Merlot, Pinotage, Chenin Blanc, Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay, Cabernet Franc","summary":"Stellenbosch is South Africa's most famous wine district and its intellectual centre. The town, founded by Simon van der Stel in 1679 and shaded by oaks, has the country's only university degree in viticulture and oenology, the Elsenburg agricultural college and the Nietvoorbij research institute. More than 200 producers farm the district's slopes, from historic estates to modern wineries.\n\nIts strength is red wine, above all Cabernet Sauvignon and Bordeaux-style blends, which gain structure and freshness from the district's granite mountains and the cooling south-easter off False Bay. Meerlust Rubicon (first made in 1980), Kanonkop Paul Sauer, Vergelegen V and Rust en Vrede's estate blend are classics, and Kanonkop's Pinotage, from vines planted in the 1950s, is the reference for the country's own grape. Old-vine Chenin Blanc from the Bottelary and Helderberg areas and Chardonnay from the higher slopes are equally serious.\n\nThe district is divided into eight wards: Banghoek, Bottelary, Devon Valley, Jonkershoek Valley, Papegaaiberg, Polkadraai Hills, Simonsberg-Stellenbosch and Vlottenburg. Much of the best-known land, including the Helderberg slopes around Somerset West (Vergelegen, Rust en Vrede, Waterford, Ernie Els), lies outside any ward and is labelled simply 'Stellenbosch'. The Stellenbosch Wine Route, founded in 1971, was South Africa's first.","terroir":"Mountains on three sides (Simonsberg, Jonkershoek, Helderberg) and False Bay to the south; about 600 to 800 mm of rain in the valley, more on the mountains. Decomposed granite on the higher slopes, Table Mountain sandstone higher still, and Malmesbury shale and alluvium on the lower ground to the west.","producers":["Kanonkop","Meerlust","Rustenberg","Vergelegen","Rust en Vrede","Thelema","Tokara","Warwick","Delheim","Jordan","Waterford","De Toren","Ken Forrester","Kleine Zalze","Simonsig","Reyneke","Alheit (sources)","Mvemve Raats","Raats","Keermont","Le Riche"],"nerd_note":"Stellenbosch's oak-lined streets are a result of Van der Stel's order to plant oaks in the 1680s; the university's experimental farm at Welgevallen is where Perold bred Pinotage in 1925.","contains":["Banghoek","Bottelary","Devon Valley","Jonkershoek Valley","Papegaaiberg","Polkadraai Hills","Simonsberg-Stellenbosch","Vlottenburg"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-stettyn":{"name":"Stettyn","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Worcester","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz","summary":"A ward in the Stettynskloof west of Worcester, home of the Stettyn cellar. It is one of seven wards in the Worcester district, a warm, irrigated area whose fruit goes largely to wine and brandy.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-still-bay":{"name":"Still Bay","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Noir","summary":"A coastal district around Stilbaai on the Garden Route, with the Goukou River Valley ward. Its vineyards, close to the Indian Ocean, are cooled by sea breezes and grow mostly Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Noir.","contains":["Goukou River Valley"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-stormsvlei":{"name":"Stormsvlei","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Swellendam","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Chenin Blanc","summary":"A ward west of Swellendam near the Riviersonderend, on the road between Robertson and the coast. Its vineyards benefit from cool air drifting up the river valley from the coast.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-sundays-glen":{"name":"Sunday's Glen","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Walker Bay","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinot Noir, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"The easternmost Walker Bay ward, beyond Stanford, a cool coastal site. Like the other new Walker Bay wards, it relies on the cooling influence of the Atlantic and on Bokkeveld shale and sandstone soils, which suit Pinot Noir and Sauvignon Blanc.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-sutherland-karoo":{"name":"Sutherland-Karoo","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Karoo-Hoogland","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Pinot Noir, Chardonnay","summary":"A high-altitude, semi-arid district around Sutherland, South Africa's coldest town and home of the national astronomical observatory, with vineyards at about 1,500 m, the highest in the country.","terroir":"Dolerite and shale soils; extreme cold in winter.","producers":["Super Single Vineyards (Mount Sutherland)"],"rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-swartberg":{"name":"Swartberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Prince Albert","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz","summary":"A ward in the Swartberg mountains above Prince Albert. Its few hectares of vines grow in a dry, high-altitude setting where cold nights preserve acidity.","rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-swartland":{"name":"Swartland","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Coastal Region","styles":["red","white","fortified","orange"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Shiraz, Grenache, Cinsault, Pinotage, Mourvèdre, Palomino","summary":"The Swartland, the 'black land', takes its name from the renosterbos (rhino bush) that once darkened its rolling wheatfields north of Cape Town. For most of its history it grew grain and supplied big co-operatives with high-yielding grapes. That changed when Charles Back of Fairview and Spice Route began buying land here in the late 1990s and a young winemaker, Eben Sadie, found old, dry-farmed bush vines of Chenin Blanc, Grenache, Cinsault and Syrah on the Paardeberg. His Columella (2000) and Palladius (2002) showed what they could do.\n\nA generation followed: Chris and Andrea Mullineux, Adi Badenhorst at Kalmoesfontein, Callie Louw at Porseleinberg, Craig Hawkins (Testalonga), Lammershoek, David and Nadia Sadie, Donovan Rall. Their Swartland Revolution festival (2010 to 2015) and the Swartland Independent Producers association, which sets rules on natural winemaking and regional sourcing, made the district shorthand for South Africa's new wave: whole-bunch Syrah, old-vine Chenin blends aged in old foudres and concrete, and skin-contact whites. The district also has eight wards, from the Paardeberg granite to the schist of the Riebeek and Porseleinberg slopes.","terroir":"Warm and dry (400 to 600 mm of rain), with mostly dry-farmed bush vines. Soils include decomposed granite (Paardeberg), Malmesbury shale and schist (Kasteelberg, Porseleinberg) and iron-rich koffieklip.","producers":["Sadie Family","Mullineux","A.A. Badenhorst","Porseleinberg","Lammershoek","David & Nadia","Testalonga","Rall","Spice Route","Swartland Winery","Kloovenburg"],"nerd_note":"Sadie's 'Old Vineyard Series' bottles single old vineyards from across the Cape, each label naming the site, such as Skerpioen, Mev. Kirsten and 'T Voetpad.","contains":["Malmesbury","Paardeberg/Perdeberg","Paardeberg South","Piket-Bo-Berg","Porseleinberg","Riebeekberg","Riebeeksrivier","St Helena Bay"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-swellendam":{"name":"Swellendam","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A district around the historic town of Swellendam (1743), the third-oldest in South Africa, with wards Buffeljags, Malgas and Stormsvlei. Its warm, dry wards lie along the lower Breede River between Robertson and the coast.","contains":["Buffeljags","Malgas","Stormsvlei"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-theewater":{"name":"Theewater","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Overberg","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Sauvignon Blanc, Chardonnay","summary":"A ward near the Theewaterskloof Dam and Villiersdorp, at the edge of the Overberg's mountains. The area's growers mainly sell fruit to cellars elsewhere.","rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-tradouw":{"name":"Tradouw","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Chardonnay","summary":"A ward around Barrydale below the Tradouw Pass. Joubert-Tradauw makes Chardonnay and Shiraz here, in one of the Klein Karoo's coolest corners, influenced by air from the coast through the Tradouw Pass.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-tradouw-highlands":{"name":"Tradouw Highlands","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinot Noir, Chardonnay, Shiraz","summary":"A higher, cooler ward in the mountains above Barrydale, whose growers make fresh whites and Pinot Noir. Its vineyards, at about 500 to 600 m, are among the coolest in the Klein Karoo.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-tulbagh":{"name":"Tulbagh","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Coastal Region","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Mourvèdre, Pinotage","summary":"A horseshoe-shaped valley enclosed by the Groot Winterhoek, Witzenberg and Obiekwaberg mountains, about 90 minutes north of Cape Town. Cold air pools on the valley floor at night (a 'cold trap'), giving large day-night temperature swings. Tulbagh's Church Street has 32 national monuments, many restored after the 1969 earthquake. The valley is known for Shiraz and Rhône blends and for Cap Classique pioneer Krone (Twee Jonge Gezellen).","terroir":"A former lake basin with varied alluvial and sandstone soils.","producers":["Saronsberg","Krone (Twee Jonge Gezellen)","Waverley Hills","Rijk's","Fable Mountain","Montpellier"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-upington":{"name":"Upington","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Northern Cape","subregion":"Central Orange River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Colombard, Chenin Blanc, Muscat","summary":"A ward on the Orange River around the town of Upington in the Central Orange River district, an irrigated desert-oasis vineyard area. The Orange River vineyards ripen very early (harvest can start in December), and most grapes go to Orange River Cellars, one of the largest wine businesses in South Africa, for Colombard, Chenin Blanc, sweet Muscat and juice.","rslug":"northern-cape"},"za-upper-hemel-en-aarde-valley":{"name":"Upper Hemel-en-Aarde Valley","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Walker Bay","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinot Noir, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Syrah","summary":"The middle section of the Hemel-en-Aarde, further inland and slightly warmer, on lighter granite-derived and shale soils. Newton Johnson, La Vierge, Restless River and Storm make some of the country's most elegant Pinot Noir.","terroir":"Decomposed granite and shale; more sheltered than the lower valley.","producers":["Newton Johnson","Restless River","Storm","La Vierge","Sumaridge"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-upper-langkloof":{"name":"Upper Langkloof","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Klein Karoo","subregion":"Klein Karoo","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Pinot Noir, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A high, cool ward in the apple-growing Langkloof valley around Haarlem in the far east of the Klein Karoo. Its cool climate suits Pinot Noir and Sauvignon Blanc.","rslug":"klein-karoo"},"za-vinkrivier":{"name":"Vinkrivier","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward along the Vink River near McGregor. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-vlottenburg":{"name":"Vlottenburg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Stellenbosch","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot, Chenin Blanc, Sauvignon Blanc","summary":"A ward south-west of Stellenbosch town around the Vlottenburg railway halt and the Eerste River, where cooling False Bay winds reach the vines in the afternoon. Its old co-operative cellar is now Stellenbosch Hills, and the ward's Bordeaux varieties and Chenin Blanc benefit from afternoon sea breezes.","terroir":"Alluvial and shale-derived soils on gentle slopes.","producers":["Stellenbosch Hills (Vlottenburg cellar)","Spier (nearby)"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-voor-paardeberg":{"name":"Voor-Paardeberg","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Paarl","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Pinotage, Cinsault","summary":"The southern and eastern side ('voor', in front of) the Paardeberg, the granite massif between Paarl and the Swartland. Old dry-land bush vines of Chenin, Cinsault and Shiraz supply many of the Cape's new-wave winemakers.","terroir":"Decomposed granite over clay, dry farmed; warm and windy.","producers":["Scali","Vondeling","Seven Springs (sources)"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-vredendal":{"name":"Vredendal","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Olifants River","subregion":"Olifants River","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Pinotage","summary":"The ward around Vredendal in the lower Olifants River, home to Namaqua Wines, one of the largest cellars in South Africa. Namaqua Wines, formed by merging the Vredendal and Spruitdrift co-operatives, is one of the country's largest producers of inexpensive bottled and boxed wine.","producers":["Namaqua Wines"],"rslug":"olifants-river"},"za-walker-bay":{"name":"Walker Bay","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Cape South Coast","subregion":"Cape South Coast","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Pinot Noir, Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Pinotage, Shiraz","summary":"The district around the whale-watching town of Hermanus, best known for the Hemel-en-Aarde ('heaven and earth') valley, where Tim Hamilton Russell planted Pinot Noir and Chardonnay in 1975 and made the Cape's first serious Burgundy-style wines. Walker Bay now has seven wards: Hemel-en-Aarde Valley, Upper Hemel-en-Aarde Valley, Hemel-en-Aarde Ridge, Bot River, Stanford Foothills, Springfontein Rim and Sunday's Glen. Its Pinotage is also highly regarded.","terroir":"Weathered Bokkeveld shale and decomposed granite; strong maritime influence and wind from Walker Bay.","producers":["Hamilton Russell","Bouchard Finlayson","Newton Johnson","Creation","Ataraxia","Southern Right","Storm","Restless River","Crystallum","Alheit"],"contains":["Hemel-en-Aarde Valley","Upper Hemel-en-Aarde Valley","Hemel-en-Aarde Ridge","Bot River","Stanford Foothills","Springfontein Rim","Sunday's Glen"],"rslug":"cape-south-coast"},"za-wellington":{"name":"Wellington","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Coastal Region","subregion":"Coastal Region","styles":["red","white","sparkling"],"grapes":"Pinotage, Shiraz, Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A district north of Paarl at the foot of the Hawequa mountains, about 45 minutes from Cape Town. It supplies more than 85 percent of South Africa's vine cuttings from its nurseries, and its 30 or so producers range from historic estates to Diemersfontein, which created 'coffee Pinotage' in 2001. Its five wards (Blouvlei, Bovlei, Groenberg, Limietberg and Mid-Berg River) were added recently.","terroir":"Alluvial terraces along the Berg River and granite and sandstone foothills; snow on the peaks in winter, cooler nights than the coast.","producers":["Diemersfontein","Bosman Family Vineyards","Mont du Toit","Andreas"],"contains":["Blouvlei","Bovlei","Groenberg","Limietberg","Mid-Berg River"],"rslug":"coastal-region"},"za-western-cape":{"name":"Western Cape","cat":"WO","subcat":"Geographical Unit","region":"National and multi-region","subregion":"Greater Cape","styles":["red","white","sparkling","fortified","sweet"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Cabernet Sauvignon, Colombard, Shiraz, Sauvignon Blanc, Pinotage, Chardonnay","summary":"The Western Cape geographical unit holds almost all of South Africa's wine grapes. 'WO Western Cape' on a label means a blend from two or more of its regions, and many large brands use it.","producers":["KWV","Distell / Heineken brands","Kleine Zalze"],"rslug":"national-and-multi-region"},"za-worcester":{"name":"Worcester","cat":"WO","subcat":"District","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Breede River Valley","styles":["red","white","fortified"],"grapes":"Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz, Muscadel","summary":"The Worcester district is the brandy capital of South Africa, with the largest distillery of its kind in the Southern Hemisphere, and a major source of bulk and branded wine. It has seven wards: Hex River Valley, Keeromsberg, Moordkuil, Nuy, Rooikrans, Scherpenheuvel and Stettyn.","producers":["Nuy","Stettyn","Alvi's Drift"],"contains":["Hex River Valley","Keeromsberg","Moordkuil","Nuy","Rooikrans","Scherpenheuvel","Stettyn"],"rslug":"breede-river-valley"},"za-zandrivier":{"name":"Zandrivier","cat":"WO","subcat":"Ward","region":"Breede River Valley","subregion":"Robertson","styles":["red","white"],"grapes":"Chardonnay, Colombard, Sauvignon Blanc, Shiraz, Cabernet Sauvignon","summary":"A ward of the Robertson district. Robertson's wards share its lime-rich soils and warm, dry, wind-cooled climate. Most Robertson wards are small, river-centred farming communities whose growers deliver to co-operative cellars such as Robertson Winery, Rooiberg and Van Loveren, and the names rarely appear on labels; the district's reputation rests on Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Cap Classique, fortified Muscadel and increasingly Shiraz and Cabernet.","rslug":"breede-river-valley"}}};
